'''Tata Semiconductor Assembly and Test Pvt. Ltd.''' ('''TSAT''')<ref>{{Cite news |date=2024-02-29 |title=India's major leap into semiconductor manufacturing: Union Cabinet nod to Rs 1.26 lakh crore chip-making units |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/union-cabinet-semiconductor-manufacturing-chip-making-plans-tata-semiconductor-assembly-pli-pm-modi/articleshow/108110063.cms |access-date=2024-08-11 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Tata Semiconductor Assembly and Test Pvt Ltd (TSAT) - Zauba Corp |url=https://www.zaubacorp.com/company/TATA-SEMICONDUCTOR-ASSEMBLY-AND-TEST-PRIVATE-LIMITED/U26104KA2020PTC133736 }}</ref> is India's first indigenous and greenfield<ref>{{cite web|author=The Hindu Bureau|title=Tata, ADI join forces to boost semiconductor ecosystem in India|website=The Hindu|date=2024-09-18|url=https://www.thehindu.com/business/tata-adi-join-forces-to-boost-semiconductor-ecosystem-in-india/article68656294.ece|access-date=2025-03-01}}</ref> semiconductor assembly and test facility [[factory]] in [[Jagiroad]].<ref name=":3">{{Cite news |date=2024-08-03 |title=Tata's Assam semiconductor plant to make 4.83 crore chips per day using indigenous tech: Ashwini Vaishnaw |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/technology/tatas-assam-semiconductor-plant-to-make-4-83-crore-chips-per-day-using-indigenous-tech-ashwini-vaishnaw/articleshow/112250831.cms?from=mdr |access-date=2024-08-11 |work=The Economic Times |issn=0013-0389}}</ref> It is further poised to become a landmark industrial project for the [[northeast India]].

The project is part of India's Semiconductor policy, supported by the India Semiconductor Mission and Assam's Electronics policy.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=2024-08-03 |title=Assam: Tata Electronics Initiates Rs 27,000 Crore Semiconductor Facility in Assam with Bhumi Pujan Ceremony |url=https://www.sentinelassam.com/north-east-india-news/assam-news/assam-tata-electronics-initiates-rs-27000-crore-semiconductor-facility-in-assam-with-bhumi-pujan-ceremony |access-date=2024-08-11 |website=Sentinel Assam |language=en}}</ref> Construction was set to begin in 2024, with the first phase ready by mid-2025.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Mishra |first=Ashutosh |title=Tata Electronics Assam chip plant to be operational in 2025: Chandrasekaran |url=https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/tata-electronics-assam-chip-plan-to-be-operational-in-2025-chandrasekaran-124080300991_1.html |access-date= |work=Business Standard}}</ref> This will greatly boost industrialization in North-East India.

== Background and Inception ==
The project was approved by the [[Union Council of Ministers|Union Cabinet]] chaired by Prime Minister [[Narendra Modi]] on 29 February 2024.<ref name=":1">{{Cite news |last=Desk |first=PTI |title=Tata's ₹27,000 crore Assam semiconductor plant to become operational in 2025, create 27,000 jobs |url=https://www.hindustantimes.com/business/tatas-rs-27-000-crore-assam-semiconductor-plant-to-become-operational-in-2025-create-27-000-jobs-101722748614802.html |work=Hindustan Times}}</ref> A meeting was held on 29 July 2024, at Janata Bhawan with officials from the [[Tata Group]] and the state government, preceding the scheduled 3 August 2024, Bhumi Pujan ceremony for the upcoming Tata Group semiconductor unit.{{fact|date=June 2025}}

The foundation of the Tata Semiconductor facility was officially laid with a groundbreaking ceremony held on 3 August 2024.<ref name=":2">{{Cite news |date=2024-08-05 |title='Bhumi Pujan' of Tata Semiconductor facility in Assam: Tata Sons chairman N Chandrasekaran conveys best wishes of Ratan Tata |url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/technology/tech-news/bhumi-pujan-of-tata-semiconductor-facility-in-assam-tata-sons-chairman-n-chandrasekaran-conveys-best-wishes-of-ratan-tata/articleshow/112249497.cms |access-date=2024-08-11 |work=The Times of India |issn=0971-8257}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-08-03 |title=Bhumi Pujan of Rs 27,000 crore semiconductor assembly and test facility conducted in Assam |url=https://indianexpress.com/article/india/bhumi-pujan-rs-27000-crore-semiconductor-assembly-test-facility-assam-9492920/ |access-date=2024-08-11 |website=The Indian Express |language=en}}</ref> The event was attended by key figures, including Assam's Chief Minister Himanta Biswa Sarma and Tata Sons Chairman N Chandrasekaran.<ref name=":2" /> The ceremony was a significant milestone, signaling the commencement of what is considered a game-changing project for the region and the entire country.{{fact|date=June 2025}}

According to the proposal, the semiconductor unit is expected to be established at erstwhile [[Panchgram|Hindustan Paper Corporation]]'s Nagaon Paper Mill premise, which has been non-operational for several years.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Tata Electronics Plans ₹40,000 Cr Investment in Assam |url=https://guwahatiplus.com/assam/tata-electronics-plans-rs-40000-cr-investment-in-assam |access-date=2024-07-30 |website=guwahatiplus.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=2024-02-29 |title=Tata's semi-conductor plant to start construction in 100 days in Assam |url=https://nenews.in/business/tatas-semi-conductor-plant-to-start-construction-in-100-days-in-assam/7679/ |access-date=2024-08-11 |website=Northeast News |language=en-US}}</ref>

== Investment and impact ==
The Tata Semiconductor facility in Jagiroad, Assam, represents a significant investment of approximately INR 27,000 crore (around US$3.6 billion).<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Tata Group to Build the Nation's First Indigenous Semiconductor Assembly and Test facility in Assam {{!}} Tata group |url=https://www.tata.com/newsroom/business/first-indian-semiconductor-assembly-test-facility |access-date=2024-08-11 |website=www.tata.com |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":1" /> This substantial financial commitment is part of Tata Electronics' strategy to develop a cutting-edge semiconductor assembly and test facility, which is expected to generate over 25,000 direct and indirect jobs in the region.{{efn|Various news outlets in India report different numbers for the estimated future direct and indirect jobs that it will provide. Hindustan Times,<ref name=":1" /> The Economic Times,<ref name=":3" /> Business Today,<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-08-05 |title=Tata Electronics' ₹27,000 Cr Semiconductor Plant: 'Bhumi Pujan' Ceremony In Assam's Jagiroad |url=https://www.businesstoday.in/bt-tv/video/tata-electronics-rs27000-cr-semiconductor-plant-bhumi-pujan-ceremony-in-assams-jagiroad-440227-2024-08-05 |access-date=2024-08-11 |website=Business Today |language=en}}</ref> and others report it as 27,000 jobs, while Times Now reports it as 30,000 jobs.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Saxena |first=Arijit |date=2024-08-03 |title=Tata Sons' Rs 27,000 Crore Semiconductor Project To Generate 30,000 Jobs In This State |url=https://www.timesnownews.com/business-economy/industry/tata-sons-rs-27000-crore-semiconductor-project-to-generate-30000-jobs-in-this-state-article-112245505 |access-date=2024-08-11 |website=Times Now |language=en}}</ref>}} This project aims to boost the local economy and advance India's position in the global semiconductor industry.<ref name=":0" />

=== Collaborations ===
On 16 April 2024, Tata Electronics and [[Tesla, Inc.|Tesla]] had been said to sign a strategic deal to procure semiconductor chips for its worldwide operations. Apart from Taiwan, China and South Korea, India is expected to join the chip supplies group soon.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2024-04-16 |title=A Tata-Tesla deal has just won India a big strategic edge |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/cons-products/electronics/a-tata-tesla-deal-has-just-won-india-a-big-strategic-edge/articleshow/109340339.cms?from=mdr |access-date=2024-12-08 |work=The Economic Times |issn=0013-0389}}</ref>

